 ## Unreleased
 
+- Fix: Honor Advanced Elements Cache opt-in on Elementor WP Menu widgets with early widget bypass and menu-item update/deletion invalidation. Shared menu HTML retains the active-page attributes of its first request.
 - Improve: Advanced Elements Cache uses the administrator's per-element opt-in as a declaration of shared output across pages and visitors, without blanket third-party version or callback allowlists. Preserve device/language variants and explicit private, preview, query and replay exclusions.
 - New: Administrator-only Advanced Elements Cache status distinguishes saved activation, supported structure and recent frontend hit/miss/bypass observations, with actionable rejection reasons.
 - Fix: Keep native preview and globally disabled cache from writing frontend cache observations.
